    "type": "mc",
    "text": "An inverse function undoes $f$: if $f(2) = 7$, then $f^(-1)(7) =$",
    "options": [
     "2",
     "7",
     "$frac{1}{7}$",
     "−2"
    ],
    "answer": 0,
    "hint": "$f$ sends 2 to 7. The inverse sends 7 back.",
    "explain": "$f^(-1)(7) = 2$"
   },
   {
    "id": "L2",
    "type": "expr",
    "text": "To find a formula: write $y = f(x)$, swap $x$ and $y$, and solve for $y$. Find $f^(-1)(x)$ for $f(x) = 2x + 3$.",
    "answer": "(x - 3)/2",
    "vars": [
     "x"
    ],
    "keys": [
